6. `conversion` : cout << (char)('A' + i) << '\n'; The `(char)` part is called a
    **type cast**. By putting `(char)` in front of the math, you are explicitly 
    telling C++: "Take the integer result of this math and force it back into a 
    character before printing it."
    

